DP  - 2014 Mar
TI  - Cerebral oximetry in cardiac anesthesia.
PG  - S60-9
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.10.22 [doi]
AB  - Cerebral oximetry based on near-infrared spectroscopy (NIRS) is increasingly used 
      during the perioperative period of cardiovascular operations. It is a noninvasive 
      technology that can monitor the regional oxygen saturation of the frontal cortex. 
      Current literature indicates that it can stratify patients preoperatively 
      according their risk. Intraoperatively, it provides continuous information about 
      brain oxygenation and allows the use of brain as sentinel organ indexing overall 
      organ perfusion and injury. This review focuses on the clinical validity and 
      applicability of this monitor for cardiac surgical patients.
