DP  - 2014 Feb
TI  - Coronary-pulmonary artery fistula-multiple diagnostic imaging modalities.
PG  - E27-9
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.12.26 [doi]
AB  - Coronary artery fistula is rare anomalies. Most adult patients are usually 
      asymptomatic. A fistula is incidentally identified in the adult using 
      echocardiography. Coronary angiography is considered the standard tool to confirm 
      a coronary artery fistula. However, multidetector computed tomography (MDCT) 
      angiography is considered a good alternative to coronary angiography.
