TI  - Publishing in open access era: focus on respiratory journals.
PG  - 564-7
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2014.03.18 [doi]
AB  - We have entered an open access publishing era. The impact and significance of 
      open access is still under debate after two decades of evolution. Open access 
      journals benefit researchers and the general public by promoting visibility, 
      sharing and communicating. Non-mainstream journals should turn the challenge of 
      open access into opportunity of presenting best research articles to the global 
      readership. Open access journals need to optimize their business models to 
      promote the healthy and continuous development.
