TI  - Video-assisted thoracic surgery (VATS) right upper lobectomy.
PG  - S280-1
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.07.15 [doi]
AB  - Video-assisted thoracic surgery (VATS) plays supplementary role to the open 
      surgery in the thoracic surgery. As the clinical education and VATS procedure 
      developed, more patients are willing to take VATS surgery than open surgery if 
      the condition permits. With the help of proficiency and HD thoracoscopic 
      instruments, nearly all open surgery can be done, theoretically, in VATS either. 
      In addition the better accessibility to the operative video and academic meeting 
      greatly propel the prevalence of VATS surgery. Here I present a VATS right upper 
      lobectomy case to communicating operative techniques.
