TI  - Temporary transection of innominate vein in surgery of midtracheal tumor.
PG  - E19-21
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2014.01.22 [doi]
AB  - In this case, a patient presented with a large primary midtracheal tumor 
      posterior to the innominate vein and brachiocephalic artery. The left innominate 
      vein (LIV) was temporarily transected to attain proper access to the tumor. After 
      complete removal of the tumor, the vessel was reanastomosed. The operation was 
      uneventful, and the patient recovered well. Temporary transection of the LIV 
      appears to be a reasonable alternative to surgical resection in such a large 
      cross-border midtracheal tumor.
