TI  - Tyrosine kinase inhibitors re-treatment beyond progression: choice and challenge.
PG  - 595-7
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2014.04.36 [doi]
AB  - Tyrosine kinase inhibitors (TKIs) are highly effective agents for the treatment 
      of lung cancer which harbors activated gene mutation. However, for patients with 
      failure of TKI, TKI re-treatment beyond progression (TRBP) is still a potential 
      option that has been proven by many literatures. In this review, we summarize the 
      clinical evidence of TRBP and discuss the potential mechanisms to overcome 
      TKI-acquired resistance.
