TI  - Non-intubated complete thoracoscopic bronchial sleeve resection for central lung 
      cancer.
PG  - 1485-8
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2014.08.10 [doi]
AB  - Bronchial sleeve resection has emerged as an effective thoracoscopic approach for 
      central lung cancer with reduced operation mortality rates, optimal lung function 
      and long-term survival. Endobronchial intubation is a commonly used method of 
      anesthesia for such thoracoscopic procedures, but is associated with increased 
      intubation-related and lung complications. Non-intubated epidural anesthesia 
      represents an alternative approach which may avoid such difficulties, 
      particularly in complicated sleeve resection situations. Here we have described a 
      case of complete endoscopic bronchial sleeve resection of right lower lung cancer 
      under non-intubated epidural anesthesia.
