TI  - Minimally invasive esophagectomy-left neck anastomosis.
PG  - 910-1
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.12.17 [doi]
AB  - Minimally invasive esophagectomy (MIE) is supplementary to open surgery in the 
      thoracic surgery. A 65-year-old male was identified with middle thoracic 
      esophageal squamous cell carcinoma by gastroscopy. In preoperative examinations, 
      neither obvious abnormality nor distant metastasis was noted, and he could 
      tolerate the esophagectomy according to his heart and lung function tests. Chest 
      computed tomography (CT) and endoscopic ultrasonography showed no visible swollen 
      lymph node in the mediastinum. The cTNM classification was T2N0M0. Therefore, MIE 
      was performed. The patient recovered well after the surgery.
