TI  - A case of heart failure due to alcoholic cardiomyopathy combined with acute 
      pulmonary embolism.
PG  - E176-80
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2014.07.32 [doi]
AB  - It has not been reported that cases of alcoholic cardiomyopathy (ACM) combined 
      with acute pulmonary embolism (PE). We hereby present a case of a 48-year-old 
      male with ACM with significant enlargement of the heart and heart failure is 
      described. Then, the patient was seized with acute PE which was confirmed by 
      specific examination and his symptoms.
