TI  - Primary mucoepidermoid carcinoma of the thymus presenting with myasthenia gravis.
PG  - E223-5
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2014.09.19 [doi]
AB  - Mucoepidermoid carcinoma (MEC) of the thymus is a rare malignant neoplasm of the 
      anterior mediastinum. There are less than 30 cases described in the English 
      literature. We report a case of a 47-year-old lady who presented with myasthenia 
      gravis and was found to have a well-circumscribed anterior mediastinal mass in 
      her medical work-up. This mass was surgically resected and subsequently found to 
      be a primary MEC of the thymus. This is the first reported case of thymic MEC 
      with concurrent myasthenia gravis. Her myasthenia symptoms have persisted 
      following complete surgical resection of her tumour.
