DP  - 2014 Sep
TI  - Calcified amorphous tumor in left atrium presenting with cerebral infarction.
PG  - 1311-4
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2014.07.46 [doi]
AB  - Calcified amorphous tumor (CAT) of the heart is an extremely rare cardiac mass. 
      We describe a case of cardiac CAT in a 70-year-old Korean female who presented 
      with acute onset dysarthria and right side weakness. Echocardiography and chest 
      computed tomography revealed a left atrial mass that originated from the 
      interatrial septum. The patient underwent surgical resection and pathologic 
      examination demonstrated CAT. Postoperative course was uneventful and she was 
      followed without recurrence.
