TI  - Video-assisted thoracolaparoscopic esophagectomy: the experience of Shanghai 
      Chest Hospital.
PG  - 906-9
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.12.14 [doi]
AB  - The traditional open esophagectomy is associated with higher morbidity, while 
      minimally invasive procedures could be accompanied with a lower one. In this 
      case, the patient is placed in the prone-decubitus position and the surgeon 
      stands in front of the patient. The "four ports" approach is adopted in the 
      thoracoscopic procedure with CO2 insufflation, and the esophagus and lymph nodes 
      are dissected. In the laparoscopic procedure, "hand assistant technique" is 
      employed. The esophagogastric anastomosis is similar with McKeown procedure.
