TI  - Early diagnosis of solitary pulmonary nodules.
PG  - 830-40
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.11.19 [doi]
AB  - Early detection of solitary pulmonary nodules (SPNs) and early treatment are of 
      great importance. However, patients with early SPNs always do not present with 
      any symptoms or signs, only to demonstrate SPNs in radiology findings. So it is 
      very critical to improve the ability to identify the SPNs, and with the 
      development of sorts of diagnostic modalities, the accuracy in the evaluation of 
      the SPNs has improved greatly. In this paper, the diagnostic methods and 
      techniques of SPNs are reviewed.
