TI  - Options for left internal mammary harvest in minimal access coronary surgery.
PG  - S638-40
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.11.02 [doi]
AB  - The left internal mammary artery (LIMA) to the left anterior descending artery 
      bypass remains the gold standard for coronary artery bypass grafting. This review 
      focuses on the three major options for LIMA takedown when using minimal access 
      options to achieve this bypass, namely standard minimally invasive direct 
      coronary artery bypass (MIDCAB), thoracoscopic MIDCAB, and robotically assisted 
      MIDCAB.
