TI  - Glomus tumor in the lung parenchyma.
PG  - 663-6
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2012.10.01 [doi]
AB  - Glomus tumors are uncommon lesions of glomus cell origin with ultrastructural and 
      immunohistochemical features of smooth muscle. In the majority of the cases 
      reported in the literature glomus tumors are benign, but there are some rare 
      cases in which they demonstrate aggressive and malignant clinical and 
      histological features. Glomangiosarcomas of the lung are extremely rare malignant 
      tumors, because of the fact that glomus bodies are rare or absent. Due to their 
      rarity they are misdiagnosed. Surgical resection is considered to be the most 
      effective treatment for this condition. We report a case of a 35 year old female 
      with a pulmonary glomangiosarcoma.
