TI  - A very early stage of obstructive fibrinous tracheal pseudo-membrane formation.
PG  - 320-2
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2012.05.10 [doi]
AB  - As result of a short-term intubation (24 hours), we report a rare and poorly 
      known complication: the formation of an obstructive fibrinous tracheal 
      pseudo-membrane (OFTP). The diagnosis and therapy of OFTP were due to its 
      spontaneous expectoration after a long asymptomatic time post extubation (four 
      days): This is a very unusual event. A CT-scan of the chest performed 3 hours 
      after intubation revealed the first step of pseudo-membrane developing.
