TI  - Primary intrapulmonary malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumor mimicking lung 
      cancer.
PG  - E155-7
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.07.02 [doi]
AB  - Malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumors (MPNSTs) are sarcomas originating from 
      the cells constituting the nerve sheaths such as Schwann cells, perineural cells 
      or fibroblasts. They represent approximately 5-10% of all soft tissue sarcomas. 
      They have been rarely observed in the lung. We describe a rare case of primary 
      lung MPNST in an elderly male patient, in which surgical approach has obtained a 
      good control of the disease. Immuno-histochemical and molecular analyses have 
      been required on the surgical specimen due to inadequate possibility of 
      recognition through morphology alone.
