TI  - Guillain-Barré syndrome in two patients with respiratory failure and a review of 
      the Japanese literature.
PG  - 601-7
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2012.11.01 [doi]
AB  - We described two patients with Guillain-Barré syndrome and respiratory failure 
      with or without mechanical ventilation. Case 1 was a 44-year-old man who treated 
      as pneumonia under mechanical ventilation for a month and transferred to our 
      hospital with unsuccessful weaning trials because of phrenic nerve palsy. Case 2 
      was a 74-year-old man who presented with aspiration pneumonia because of bulbar 
      palsy. The present two cases with review of the Japanese literature showed that 
      antecedent infection with initial symptoms within the most recent 5 to 46 days is 
      a clinical clue to the diagnosis even in patients with Guillain-Barré syndrome 
      accompanied by respiratory failure.
