TI  - Circulating tumor cells in non-small cell lung carcinoma.
PG  - 456-8
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2012.08.21 [doi]
AB  - Circulating tumor cells (CTCs) are associated with survival of cancer patients. 
      Several methods have been developed to detect circulating tumor cells. The number 
      of CTCs in NSCLC is lower than in other solid tumors. To date, trials are ongoing 
      for a better understanding of CTCs. Besides association with prognosis, CTCs can 
      be used to assess the efficacy of treatment and they are important substrates for 
      molecular profiling of the tumor..
