TI  - MicroRNA from tuberculosis RNA: A bioinformatics study.
PG  - 296-7
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2012.05.08 [doi]
AB  - The role of microRNA in the pathogenesis of pulmonary tuberculosis is the 
      interesting topic in chest medicine at present. Recently, it was proposed that 
      the microRNA can be a useful biomarker for monitoring of pulmonary tuberculosis 
      and might be the important part in pathogenesis of disease. Here, the authors 
      perform a bioinformatics study to assess the microRNA within known tuberculosis 
      RNA. The microRNA part can be detected and this can be important key information 
      in further study of the pathogenesis of pulmonary tuberculosis.
