TI  - Successful treatment of primary pulmonary melanoma.
PG  - 207-8
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2011.04.02 [doi]
AB  - Presented is a rare case of a primary melanoma of the lung in an 89 year old male 
      patient. Primary melanoma of the lung has been previously reported in the English 
      literature in about 30 patients. Surgical resection either with lobectomy of 
      pneumonectomy and a lymph node dissection has been shown to be the best chance of 
      long term survival. This is the oldest patient on record where surgical resection 
      was successful.
