TI  - Current costs of video-assisted thoracic surgery (VATS) lobectomy.
PG  - S190-3
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.07.13 [doi]
AB  - Video-assisted thoracoscopic lobectomy has many benefits over open surgery such 
      as smaller incisions, less pain, less blood loss, faster postoperative recovery, 
      shortened hospital stay, similar or superior survival rates. In contrast 
      video-assisted thoracic surgery (VATS) has higher equipment costs, increased 
      operating room times, at least initially, and a learning curve for the team. 
      However when an experienced surgeon performs the surgery, significant hospital 
      savings combined with better outcomes are achieved by video-assisted 
      thoracoscopic lobectomy.
