TI  - Pulmonary tumor thrombotic microangiopathy from metastatic epithelioid 
      angiosarcoma.
PG  - E107-11
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2012.10.08 [doi]
AB  - The lung is most common site for metastatic disease via hematogenous route. Tumor 
      emboli of the vessels of the lung induces fibrocellular and fibromuscular intimal 
      proliferation. These histopathological changes may cause pulmonary tumor 
      trombotic microangiopaty. Few cases are diagnosed antemortem. We report a 60 year 
      old woman with by metastatic epithelioid angiosarcoma involving the lung. Tumor 
      cells were positive for VEGF and topoisomerase II. VEGF may be involved in the 
      pathogenesis pulmonary tumor trombotic microangioapy and topoisomerase II 
      positivity showed sensitivity against catalytic topoisomerase II inhibitors.
