TI  - Pulmonary enteric adenocarcinoma with villin brush border immunoreactivity: a 
      case report and literature review.
PG  - E17-20
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2012.06.06 [doi]
AB  - Pulmonary enteric adenocarcinoma, a rare histologic type of primary pulmonary 
      adenocarcinoma with only 16 cases reported to date, has to be differentiated from 
      metastatic colorectal carcinoma. Here we report a case of pulmonary enteric 
      adenocarcinoma which shows villin immunoreactivity in the brush border of tumor 
      cells. As a marker for gastrointestinal adenocarcinoma, villin has been rarely 
      found positive like this pattern in pulmonary adenocarcinomas. This case suggests 
      brush border immunoreactivity of villin is possible in some cases of pulmonary 
      enteric adenocarcinomas. We suggest pathological practitioners pay attention to 
      it.
