TI  - Double whammy - mediastinal and ovarian teratoma: a rare clinical co-existence.
PG  - 434-6
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2012.03.09 [doi]
AB  - Teratomas are germ cell tumours arising as the result of abnormal development of 
      totipotential cells. They are commonly encountered in the gonads and occasionally 
      found in mediastinum. We report a case of asymptomatic 28 years old lady with 
      concomitant mature cystic teratoma in her mediastinum and left ovary which was 
      diagnosed incidentally during health check up. This case is reported because of 
      its rare and unusual coexistence.
