TI  - Corticosteroid monotherapy in a case of bronchocentric granulomatosis with a 
      two-year follow-up.
PG  - E207-9
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.10.13 [doi]
AB  - Bronchocentric granulomatosis (BCG) is a rare disease. Because of the possibility 
      of fungal infection, BCG has usually been treated with corticosteroids and 
      antifungal agent. However, fungi are not detected in all BCG tissues. We report a 
      case of proven BCG by open lung biopsy without fungi in a woman with 
      corticosteroids monotherapy and two-year follow-up.
