DP  - 2013 Oct
TI  - Recent advances in radiotherapy for thoracic tumours.
PG  - S551-5
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.08.46 [doi]
AB  - Radiation Oncology technology has continued to advance at a rapid rate and is 
      bringing significant benefits to patients. This review outlines some of the 
      advances in technology and radiotherapy treatment of thoracic cancers including 
      brachytherapy, stereotactic radiotherapy, tomotherapy and intensity modulated 
      radiotherapy. The importance of functional imaging with PET and management of 
      movement are highlighted. Most of the discussion relates to non-small cell lung 
      cancer but management of mesothelioma and small cell lung cancer are also 
      covered. This technology has substantial benefits to patients in terms of 
      decreasing toxicity both in the short and longer term.
