TI  - Adjuvant chemotherapy and radiotherapy in the treatment of non-small cell lung 
      cancer (NSCLC).
PG  - S371-7
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.05.16 [doi]
AB  - Lung cancer is one of the most common human malignancies and remains the leading 
      cause of cancer related deaths worldwide. Many recent technological advances led 
      to improved diagnostics and staging of lung cancer. With development of new 
      treatment options such as targeted therapies there might be improvement in 
      progression free survival of patients with advanced stage non-small cell lung 
      cancer (NSCLC). Improvement in overall survival is still reserved for selected 
      patients and selected treatments. One of the mostly investigated therapeutic 
      options is adjuvant treatment. There are many open issues in selection of 
      patients and administration of appropriate adjuvant treatment.
