TI  - Complete thoracoscopic lobectomy and mediastinal lymph node dissection.
PG  - S308-9
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.07.46 [doi]
AB  - To evaluate the complete thoracoscopic lower right lobectomy and mediastinal 
      lymph node. During the surgery, the lower right pulmonary artery and vein, 
      bronchi and lymph nodes were treated using a unidirectional approach. Eight 
      stations (2, 3, 4, 7, 8, 9, 10 and 11) of lymph nodes were dissected completely 
      en bloc. Repeated stretch and flipping was avoided in this procedure, which was 
      beneficial for the unaffected side of the lung. The operation of lymph node 
      dissection was completed thoroughly in accordance with standard principles.
