DP  - 2013 Aug
TI  - Is pneumothorax after acupuncture so uncommon?
PG  - E144-6
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2013.08.18 [doi]
AB  - Acupuncture is one of the most widely used forms of traditional Chinese medicine 
      often referred to as alternative therapy in the Western World and over the past 
      decades it has become increasingly popular in Denmark. Pneumothorax is known as 
      the most common serious complication following acupuncture, but it is quite 
      rarely reported. During a three-month period two patients with pneumothorax 
      caused by acupuncture were admitted to our department. The purpose of this case 
      report is to increase awareness of this complication, which may not be so 
      uncommon.
