TI  - Peripartum acute aortic dissection: A case report & review of literature.
PG  - 65-7
LID - 10.3978/j.issn.2072-1439.2010.11.12 [doi]
AB  - Acute aortic dissection is a rare clinical entity that mainly affects patients 
      older than 50 years. It is unusual in younger patients and its presence has been 
      traditionally associated with trauma, Marfan syndrome, bicuspid aortic valve and 
      pregnancy. We present here, a case of a 30 year old pregnant female with acute 
      aortic dissection type A (De Bakey II), without family history of connective 
      tissue diseases and signs of Marfan syndrome.
